  "prefLabel": "He-A 708.03 Follow-Up Visit",
  "priorExpiration": "2006-11-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-A 708.03 Follow-Up Visit. If adjudged necessary by the department representative because of needs for correction as a result of a previous site visit, client complaints, or errors in paperwork, a follow-up visit to communicate and discuss concerns shall be conducted, to ensure that the provider has followed the recommendations for improvements and changes, and for corrective actions.\n\nSource. #6653, EMERGENCY, eff 12-12-97, EXPIRED 4-11-98\n\nNew. #6753, eff 5-20-98; ss by #8624, INTERIM, eff 5-20-06, EXPIRES: 11-16-06; ss by #8749, eff 11-16-06",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-a700.html"
